WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:45.820
[Music]

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:50.580
[Narrator:] The typical chancre is raised,
indurated, sharply circumscribed,

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:54.100
frequently ulcerated, usually has satellite buboes,

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:58.020
and is not particularly painful unless there is secondary infection.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:06.720
Chancres frequently are not typical and may be multiple. Suspect any genital lesion.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:13.380
In every case of urethral discharge, palpate the urethra for possible intra-urethral chancre.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:18.959
Follow every case of gonorrhea with blood tests for four months to rule out syphilis.

00:01:18.959 --> 00:01:23.119
Look for cervical chancre. Some are atypical,

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:29.120
consisting merely of diffuse enlargement and induration of the entire cervix.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:34.480
Extragenital chancres occur on the lip,
tonsil, breast, and elsewhere.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:39.840
Do darkfields on suspicion, and blood tests routinely.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.820
Look for chancre of the finger in doctors and nurses.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.340
They are painful and often not as typical as this one.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.900
They frequently resemble an ordinary paronychia.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:54.800
This lesion and those following are not syphilitic.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.540
Darkfield examinations should be performed

00:01:57.569 --> 00:02:02.929
on every genital lesion and on all suspected extragenital lesions.

00:02:02.929 --> 00:02:04.709
If repeated darkfields are negative,

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.760
follow with blood tests for four months to rule out syphilis.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:14.760
Take a blood test at least once a week for the first two months, and once a month for the next two months.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:26.280
Differential diagnosis of primary syphilis
depends largely upon darkfield examination.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.960
To prepare the lesion for obtaining a specimen,

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:36.280
soak a piece of gauze in normal saline solution and rub hard to produce slight abrasion.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:44.190
After the surface of the lesion has been cleansed and abraded, blot it with a dry piece of gauze

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:48.780
and wait a few seconds for serum to ooze from the surface.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:55.860
Now touch a clean, dry slide to the serum and cover specimen with a clean, dry cover slip.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:03.950
The specimen is now ready to be placed under the darkfield microscope for examination.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:11.940
Spirochete pallida resembles many non-pathogenic spirilla, therefore darkfield examination

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:17.850
should be undertaken only by one who is thoroughly experienced in this procedure.

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:22.460
In localities where persons experienced in
darkfield technique are not available,

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:24.940
the delayed darkfield technique is useful.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:32.520
The specimen of serum is drawn into a capillary tube, the ends sealed, and the tube mailed immediately.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:44.320
Most state health departments provide for
examination of delayed darkfield specimens.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:49.290
Do not use darkfield examination for lesions inside the mouth,

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:55.040
unless the specimen is taken by aspiration rather than from the surface of the lesion.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:04:01.069
Some normal mouth spirochetes cannot be distinguished from spirochete pallida.

00:04:01.069 --> 00:04:03.469
If the lesion is on the outer surface of the lip,

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.780
cleanse the surface carefully before taking the specimen.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:11.900
Specimens may also be obtained by aspiration of serum from the base of a lesion.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:18.900
One tenth cc of normal saline is injected and withdrawn.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:26.130
A single negative darkfield examination does not exclude syphilis.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:30.720
Chancres are apt to be darkfield-negative if topical applications have been used,

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:34.560
if the patient has received anti-syphilitic
treatment of any kind,

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.520
or if the lesion has been present more than a month or six weeks.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:42.560
At least three or four negative specimens
should be obtained

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:46.571
before a suspected lesion is considered darkfield-negative.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:52.580
On the other hand, a positive darkfield establishes the diagnosis of syphilis

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:54.780
even while the blood test is still negative.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:02.260
Time is of the essence in the diagnosis of syphilis.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:07.400
Let us assume an exposure to syphilis or gonorrhea, or both, at this point.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.120
In three to six days there may be evidence of gonorrhea.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:15.620
Both smears and cultures should be made.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:18.860
As early as ten days after exposure, the chancre may appear.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:22.660
It usually develops in about 21 days,

00:05:22.669 --> 00:05:27.209
although its appearance may be delayed as long as three months.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:30.160
A darkfield examination should be employed.

00:05:30.169 --> 00:05:34.929
A negative darkfield, of course, does not exclude syphilis.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.480
From six to nine weeks after exposure,

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:41.110
the blood test may be expected to assume diagnostic significance.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.620
Again, a single negative should not be relied upon.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.220
The case should be followed for at least four months

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:53.639
before concluding that infection has not resulted from the exposure.

00:05:53.639 --> 00:05:59.059
The control of early syphilis, and the prevention of congenital syphilis and late manifestations,

00:05:59.059 --> 00:06:06.059
depend on careful and painstaking attention to the time element, and on a high index of suspicion.

00:06:08.009 --> 00:06:13.580
During the secondary stage of syphilis, the
organism is disseminated throughout the body.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:17.100
This gives rise to a constitutional reaction
with general malaise

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:21.200
and aching of the bones and joints.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:27.050
Sore throat may be prominent. There is usually a generalized lymph adenopathy.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:33.180
Macular syphilids are salmon or rose-colored.

00:06:38.509 --> 00:06:43.430
If natural daylight cannot be used, the light from a blue bulb will often reveal

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:48.249
a macular rash which would be invisible in light from an ordinary bulb.

00:06:48.249 --> 00:06:51.269
Involvement of the palms and soles is particularly suggestive.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:56.760
Secondary syphilids are often papular.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:10.500
Angular lesions should always suggest syphilis to the physician.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:16.539
They frequently coalesce and assume a serpiginous appearance.

00:07:16.539 --> 00:07:22.659
It is not uncommon for the hair to fall out
in patches, giving it a moth-eaten appearance.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:28.300
Mucus patches occur in the mouth or nose or on the genitalia.

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:33.280
They are usually about one-half to two centimeters in diameter, sharply circumscribed,

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:36.720
pink, and slightly raised from the surrounding surface.

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:39.560
Ordinarily, they are not painful.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:45.040
Moist papules also known as condyloma lata occur on moist contiguous surfaces of the skin.

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:50.321
They are raised from the surrounding surface and are round and flat on top.

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:54.640
Venereal warts are not syphilitic lesions.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:59.460
They differ from moist papules in that they are flat on the sides rather than on top.

00:08:01.039 --> 00:08:06.619
The split papules shown here are large, but often they are so small as to be overlooked easily.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:11.560
Split papules may be the only sign
of secondary syphilis.

00:08:11.569 --> 00:08:13.749
Darkfield examination is positive.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:19.780
In cases of iritis, the physician should think first of atropine and second of a blood test.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:24.620
Many cases are due to secondary syphilis.

00:08:24.629 --> 00:08:30.789
The symptoms and signs of early meningeal neurosyphilis are those of any acute meningitis.

00:08:30.789 --> 00:08:36.200
This condition is distinguished by the positive
spinal fluid serologic test for syphilis.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:42.260
It often follows a lapse in treatment for early syphilis, and in such cases is called neuro-recurrence.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:48.820
Darkfield examination is useful in secondary syphilis as well as in primary syphilis.

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:53.110
A diagnosis of primary or secondary syphilis should always be confirmed

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:57.190
either by positive darkfield or positive blood tests.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:03.160
To obtain a specimen for blood test, a tourniquet is first applied to the upper arm.

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:06.080
If the veins are not prominent, one is located by palpation.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:09.480
The overlying skin is cleansed with alcohol.

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:14.260
The operator's left thumb draws the skin taut,
and the needle is inserted through the skin

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:17.800
at an acute angle and lowered until almost
parallel with the vein.

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:21.500
The vein is entered and blood withdrawn.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:53.550
The blood is placed in a clean, dry test tube.

00:10:01.130 --> 00:10:05.710
The tube is stoppered with a clean, dry cork, carefully labeled and prepared for mailing.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:08.960
Do not use soap to clean test tubes for this purpose.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:12.800
Any residual of soap will cause hemolysis of the blood.

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:22.320
Congenital syphilis is transmitted from mother to fetus in utero,

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:24.980
usually about the fifth month of pregnancy.

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:30.580
Frequently the fetus dies and a miscarriage or stillbirth results.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:36.860
The infant with active early congenital syphilis is fretful and often has snuffles.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:42.350
Crusted lesions about the mouth and nose are frequently observed.

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:51.860
There may be a generalized eruption and moist papules about the anus and genitalia.

00:10:54.720 --> 00:11:00.700
The diagnosis should be confirmed by darkfield examination of the lesions, or by blood tests, or by both.

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:08.420
Apparently well babies of both treated and untreated syphilitic mothers should be followed for at least two years.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:14.660
Perform blood tests at monthly intervals for six months and every six months thereafter.

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:18.800
In the absence of other evidence, a diagnosis of syphilis should not be made on the basis

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:22.780
of positive blood tests taken when the child is less than two months old,

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:26.060
unless quantitative tests reveal a rising titer.

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:30.060
Congenital syphilis can be prevented by treating infected mothers,

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:33.460
but first the infected mothers must be found.

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:37.720
Take a blood test as soon as pregnancy is suspected.

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:40.600
Repeat at least once later in pregnancy.

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:45.520
Take a blood test as a routine part of physical examinations before marriage.

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:50.500
More than half of the cases of syphilis so discovered will have been unsuspected.

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:57.050
Blood tests before marriage are the particular responsibility of the private physician

00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:59.630
to whom most couples go.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:05.180
A blood test experienced impresses itself on the minds of the young people.

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:09.750
If it is accompanied by a physical examination, and if the full significance of the procedure

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:14.730
is brought home to the couple, an important
relationship is established with the physician.

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:19.970
Later, when pregnancy occurs, the physician is afforded the opportunity not only to meet

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:24.800
the threat of congenital syphilis but also
to provide general pre-natal care.

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:28.860
Thus the private practitioner plays a vital
and fundamental part

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:33.360
in both medical and epidemiologic aspects of syphilis control.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:39.100
Personalized education by him vitalizes the mass program of the health department.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:43.960
Every case of syphilis comes from another case.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:49.180
To break this chain of infection, all contact, whether familial or non-familial,

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:53.420
should be examined by the physician, or for him by the health department.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:58.200
Prostitution is another...link in
the chain of infection.

00:12:58.220 --> 00:13:02.680
Physicians can help to break this link by demanding that law enforcement officers

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:09.380
vigorously enforce all laws prohibiting prostitution, procurement, solicitation, and assignation.

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:15.590
Periodic examination of prostitutes does not retard the spread of venereal diseases,

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:20.540
and it involves the physician as an accessory to the fact.

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:25.680
Nothing short of total war on vice will break
this link in the chain of infection.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:30.560
To keep abreast of current developments in the diagnosis, treatment,

00:13:30.560 --> 00:13:36.120
and public health aspects of syphilis, read Venereal Disease Information, one of the medical journals

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:39.120
published by the United States Public Health Service.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:14:39.660
[Music]

